commit 4043b296d98b629bd45ab0f6c076a3be0a5e33e5
Author: Cristian Ortega <153694889+crisnc100@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 08:42:25 2026 -0500

    Tests: review gate settings as rows, a save bar and a paths page (test-only)
    
    Test files only. These fail until the settings rows land; the code
    follows in its own commit.
    
    Changed assertions in tests/packs-review-settings.mjs, and what each
    still guards:
    - choices() reads `.pk-tabs button` (was `.pk-choice-row button`): the
      same four merge, three security and two cross-vendor choices in plain
      words, the saved one pressed.
    - "…each with its one line" -> "one line, for the selected choice only":
      still checks the selected line's exact text, plus an explicit absence
      check for every other choice's line.
    - "…its Now line, with what it needs: the gh CLI, and CI checks" and
      "…the line that holds whatever you pick" -> no gh/CI line or merge.mjs
      text while gh is not reported missing (explicit absence); a new block
      checks the amber gh line shows when gh is missing and the pick is not Off.
    - "R4: Always needs you lists the built-ins and the risky paths" and
      "…your own paths in one box … with a Preview button" -> the pack page
      shows the count and Edit paths, with no box and no lists there; the
      paths page (C9) shows both read-only lists item by item and one
      labelled, empty box, with no Preview button.
    - "R5: Cross-vendor checks … each with its line" -> Prefer pressed, its
      exact line, and Off's line absent.
    - "R7: one line names where the other review settings live" -> the
      footer reads exactly "Saved in <file>", no button when Files has no
      entry, and no "Saved as"/"Other review settings" line.
    - "every button is a styled kind" -> styled kind or a `.pk-tab` segment
      (ui-words' named control).
    - "QA 2: every choice … opens the one preview at once" -> every choice
      names itself in the save bar with nothing previewed, and Preview and
      save shows its diff, nothing written.
    - "choosing Low-risk PRs shows the file and its diff first" -> the same
      file, diff and nothing-written checks, after Preview and save.
    - "QA 3: while it waits, Now … After Save …" -> the row's one line is the
      pick's, and no Now or After Save line.
    - "a second change joins the same preview" -> the bar counts both; the
      one preview holds both diffs.
    - "Cancel drops the whole pending preview" -> both the bar's and the
      preview's Cancel restore the saved choices and write nothing.
    - "Preview of your paths", "typed paths, then a choice", "QA 4", "paths
      edited after their preview": the same trims, joins, refresh message
      and no-write checks, driven from the paths page and its save bar.
    - "a stale preview: the refusal is shown" keeps its checks; it now also
      checks the preview is dropped and the bar asks to preview again.
    - QA 5 and R7's Open in Files: same checks through the bar and the
      footer (`.pk-set-foot`, was `.pk-other`).
    
    tests/packs-security.mjs:
    - "labelled in plain words": the row's name is exactly "Security pass"
      (was a regex for "Security pass in PR reviews").
    - "the level in force is the pressed one": Off pressed, its one line
      exactly, and the other levels' text absent (was a "Now:" regex).
    - "every button is a styled kind (secondary)": every level is a
      `.pk-tab` in one role=group control.
    - clicking a level now opens the save bar (new check); the diff, Save,
      Cancel, write and stale checks run after Preview and save, unchanged.
    
    tests/ui-words.mjs:
    - drops the 'security pass "on" button' (`.btn.pk-sec-on`) contrast
      entry: that orange-outlined button is gone; a picked segment uses the
      --text token, which the token contrast tests cover. Adds the amber gh
      line (`.pk-set-warn`) to the same text-contrast check.

